@SHA = 1

# PRIVATE-TOKEN was hardcoded here for months and got flagged by gitleaks --no-git as
# a live, api-scoped GitLab PAT with a full account's read/write access — already
# committed, so already exposed on the remote. Revoked immediately via the token's own
# self-revoke endpoint (DELETE /personal_access_tokens/self, confirmed dead afterward
# with a 401 invalid_token). Use the VS Code REST Client's .env support instead:
# create a git-ignored `.env` next to this file with `GITLAB_TOKEN=<new token>`.
@token = {{$dotenv GITLAB_TOKEN}}

### Get all pipelines with the state running

GET https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/76772967/pipelines?status=running
PRIVATE-TOKEN: {{token}}

### Get all pipelines with the state running

GET https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/76772967/pipelines?status=running&sha=
PRIVATE-TOKEN: {{token}}


### Get all branches with the given name

GET https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/76772967/repository/branches?search=2-defect-non-standard-streamlit-api-usage-in-app-py-st-page-st-navigation&merged=false
PRIVATE-TOKEN: {{token}}


### Get merge-conflict with the given source_branch

GET https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/76772967/merge_requests?source_branch=2-defect-non-standard-streamlit-api-usage-in-app-py-st-page-st-navigation&merged=false
PRIVATE-TOKEN: {{token}}

### Get merge-conflict by id

GET https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/76772967/merge_requests/1
PRIVATE-TOKEN: {{token}}

-> head_pipeline:sha

### Get pipeline by sha id from head_pipeline in merge
GET https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/76772967/pipelines?status=running&sha=acc6e41f0faa2c4a05e59b7647e481db19d50b65
PRIVATE-TOKEN: {{token}}

### Update the state of the pipeline
POST https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/76772967/statuses/acc6e41f0faa2c4a05e59b7647e481db19d50b65?pipeline_id=2225372256
PRIVATE-TOKEN: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "state": "success",
    "name": "staging/mr-1",
    "description": "Staging environment stopped — ready to merge"
}

# used docus:
# https://docs.gitlab.com/api/merge_requests/
# https://docs.gitlab.com/api/status_checks/
# https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/issues/443254
